  "body": "PR #2705 fixed #2561 and is merged. Its reviews left these notes. None is a blocker. None gives an unsafe toolpath.\n\n## Behaviour\n\n- At an inside acute corner of less than about 75 degrees, the tab clearance holds a piece that it does not need to hold. The result is safe but leaves more material than necessary.\n- `core()` in `crates/motion/src/machining2d/tab_kerf.rs` skips a segment whose span is NaN. Decide if a NaN span must refuse the operation with a diagnostic instead.\n\n## Missing tests\n\n- No test covers a tabbed contour with an Arc lead or a Tangential lead.\n- No test covers tabbed levels that are off the depth grid.\n- No test covers the pick at (28, 18) that the second review names.\n\n## Wording\n\n- The module doc of `tab_kerf.rs` must say: \"at most the first D/2 of the core adjacent to the end kerf; the W + D window of tab_bridge includes it\".\n\n## Sources\n\n- Second review, round 2: comment 7008822492 on PR #2705.\n- Second review, round 3: comment 7010028455 on PR #2705.\n\nThe work can change a toolpath. Thus the effort is `effort:high` by the safety floor.\n",
